title: "kakehashi: A Sign–Concept Mapper for Japanese"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Küster
    given-names: Marc Wilhelm
    email: marc@budabe.eu
repository-code: "https://github.com/mwkuster/kakehashi"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 0.1.0.0
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX   # add after the Zenodo release
# date-released: YYYY-MM-DD
keywords:
  - Japanese
  - kanji
  - writing systems
  - grapholinguistics
  - script transfer
  - property graph
abstract: >-
  A research instrument that makes the implicit sign–reading–lexeme–concept
  mapping of the Japanese writing system explicit, queryable and testable as a
  Neo4j property graph. Built for the Grafematik 2026 article "Writing Systems
  as Cultural Maps: Semantic Alignment in Script Transfer".
